Why this patch is needed
------------------------
On a Mac the OpenSceneGraph build always forgets OPENGL_gl_LIBRARY and OPENGL_INCLUDE_DIR and then looks for Apple's
OpenGL framework. The Metal build must link ANGLE's OpenGL ES library (libGLESv2) and use ANGLE's headers, so those two
values given on the command line have to survive.

The new option OSG_KEEP_OPENGL_LIBRARY (default OFF, so nothing changes without it) skips the two UNSET lines.
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 2735c24..a24627c 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -248,8 +248,13 @@ IF(APPLE)
         # Note that without this check, libosg would use Cocoa/OpenGL but
         # libosgViewer would use X11/OpenGL, which causes compatibility
         # issues for applications using OSG.
-        UNSET(OPENGL_gl_LIBRARY CACHE)
-        UNSET(OPENGL_INCLUDE_DIR CACHE)
+        # OSG_KEEP_OPENGL_LIBRARY: the caller names an OpenGL ES library (ANGLE's) and its headers on the command line
+        # and they are used as given. Without it, this folder only finds Apple's OpenGL framework.
+        OPTION(OSG_KEEP_OPENGL_LIBRARY "Keep OPENGL_gl_LIBRARY and OPENGL_INCLUDE_DIR as given on the command line (Apple)" OFF)
+        IF(NOT OSG_KEEP_OPENGL_LIBRARY)
+            UNSET(OPENGL_gl_LIBRARY CACHE)
+            UNSET(OPENGL_INCLUDE_DIR CACHE)
+        ENDIF()
         IF(OSG_WINDOWING_SYSTEM STREQUAL "X11")
           FIND_PACKAGE(X11)
           IF(NOT X11_FOUND)
